+# Q3 revenue drop
+
+East had the largest Q2→Q3 revenue decline of any region: revenue fell from $333,747.57 to $234,325.08, down $99,422.49 (−29.8%). Ledger Pro accounts for most of it. East's Ledger Pro revenue went from $106,520.77 in Q2 to $23,015.24 in Q3, a loss of $83,505.53, which is 84% of the region's drop. The fall came from volume, not price. East logged about 100 completed Ledger Pro sales a month in Q2 and only 22–28 a month in July–September, while the unit price stayed near $48. Other regions' Ledger Pro volume held steady. East's sales recovered in Q4. The North (−4.3%) and South (−1.0%) dips were small, and Central and West grew. Revenue is units × unit_price over completed rows, with refunds (negative units) included. Note that the export contains rows dated through 2026-12-31, so the Q4 figure covers dates after this report was written (2026-10-18).
+
+| Quarter | East revenue |
+|---------|-------------:|
+| Q1 | $333,565.48 |
+| Q2 | $333,747.57 |
+| Q3 | $234,325.08 |
+| Q4 | $305,168.76 |
